README		- This
GraphicsGems	- Source code from the books "Graphics Gems I & II"
		  (GraphicsGems/GemsI and GraphicsGems/GemsII)
atomart.tar.gz	- Raytracer that does nothing but spheres and planes
book.Z		- The Issac (nee Robert) Nathanual Zebede Stanlislaws Predergast
		  joke book.
chess20.tar.gz	- Chess pieces in OFF format - these are better quality than
		  the ones in vort.
images/*	- Some images produced by the VORT raytracer (Sun rasterfile
		  format)
images/ppm/*	- Some 24bit ppm images produced mainly by the VORT raytracer,
		  and some classics like lenna and mandril.
images/haines/*	- Erich Haines' Pictures (from his MS and SPD)
movies/*	- Some movies produced by the VORT raytracer (VORT 8-bit
		  colourmapped format)
contrib/*	- various thing that have been sent to us. At the moment this
		  mainly consists of input files (scenes, geometry files,
		  tilepatterns, and a whole lot of usefull furniture items)
		  for art (the VORT raytracer) - see the subdirectory artscenes.
		  If you grab VORT this is a must get.
nff/*		- Eric Haines NFF and SPD stuff plus some nff files in the
		  directory nff/nff_files
SPD.3.0.shar.Z  - Eric Haines NFF and SPD .......
nff2art1.0.c	- Convert NFF files to (old art) art 1.0  input files
nff2art2.0.c	- Convert NFF files to (new art) art 2.0  input files
off/*		- Directory containing OFF files and programs
off.tar.gz	- The whole lot of the above OFF directory
offdisp.tar.gz	- Sunview program for displaying OFF files.
oort10.tar.gz	- object oriented ray-tracer.
oort10.txt
oort10.zip
pc/*		- A vi, lex, yacc, and make program.
preview.c	- NFF previewer using VOGLE (get vogle.tar.gz as well)
papers/*	- A collection of papers relating to graphics
send_beer	- VERY USEFUL UTILITY SCRIPT.
send_beer.el	- VERY USEFUL EMACS UTILITY SCRIPT.
thack.tar.gz	- A game.
vogle.tar.gz	- A device independent 3D graphics library.
		  (mailing list: vogle@ecr.mu.oz.au)
voglew.zip	- Vogle compiled for windoze. (BC++ 2.0)
vogl.tar.gz	- A device independent 3D graphics library based on VOGLE that
		  tries to be a subset of SGI-GL. If you write programs using
		  VOGL then they should work unchanged on an SGI.
		  (mailing list: vogle@ecr.mu.oz.au)
vopl.tar.gz	- A graph plotting library and program using vogle (only 2D yet)
vopl_patch.1	- A patch to gpp to stop it barfing when it finds blank lines
		  at the end of the file.
vopl_patch.2	- Fix to the above fix.
vvopl.tar.gz    - An Iris GL version of vopl.
vort.tar.gz	- The whole lot of what is in the vort directory above. 
		  This is the *most* up to date version, the patches do not
		  need to be applied.
gzip-1.2.4.tar	- the source for gzip, which uncompresses the .gz files.
ArtForTheMac.sea.Hqx - Macintosh version of art with display program, beta
		release.
ArtForTheMac.README - README information on the above.

oldvort.tar.gz	- the old version of the above.

offfile.ftpsites - ftp sites with off files useful in vort.
vorttoppm.c	- Converts VORT files to ppm files (doesn't need pbmplus)
ppmtovort.c	- Converts ppm files to VORT files (doesn't need pbmplus)
oldvort.tar.gz	- vort version 1.1
simplex.c	- A simple X11 'hello, world' program (origin unknown)
athena/eBones-p9.tar.gz	- Eric's (Bond Uni) version of MIT's Kerberos/bones
		      with his own DES code and all the auth. code re installed.
			(Correspondence to eay@psych.psy.uq.oz.au)
athena/eBones-p9-des.tar.gz - Eric's DES code library
			(Correspondence to eay@psych.psy.uq.oz.au)
sun-gif.tar.gz	- A sunview based GIF file viewer.
xgif.tar.gz	- An X11 based GIF viewer. (Probably not the latest version).
xfract.tar.gz	- X11 based fractal program.
hershey.tar.gz	- The Hershey font library taken from VOGL (see above).
		  Runs with VOGL or SGI-GL.

libRT.tar.gz	- a ray tracing library with a parser for the NFF grammer.
		Has several different acceleration techniques in it and
		should be relatively simple to add more, useful for people
		investigating ray tracing...

seattle.txt	- the text of a letter sent by the American Indian Chief, 
		Seattle, to the president of the United States, in 1854. 
		Food for thought...

All problems and inquiries may be reported to echidna@ecr.mu.oz.au.
